## Audit

Read the pinned Java `ResponseFuture.java` and `SemaphoreReleaseOnlyOnce.java`
from the exact source commit, then compared them with the Rust implementation,
fixture, and Phase 3/6 crosswalks. Java's two constructors and 20 public
methods are present in `fixtures/remoting/response-future-api.json`; Rust
represents the constructor overloads with nullable owned values and keeps the
transport-owned permit constructor private. The callback/result ordering,
timeout comparison, setter-versus-latch behavior, wait/put response behavior,
and release-once semantics have named fixture-backed regressions. Existing
compatibility notes cover only JVM-thread interruption and unstable Java
identity text as runtime/diagnostic differences. No new source/API mismatch
was found in this slice.

This closes only the ResponseFuture reverse-source slice. Broad P18-V01
source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow and reverse-export reconciliation
remains PARTIAL; remote Ubuntu CI, native Windows runtime, and Phase 19
Broker/Docker evidence remain open.
